# env-sovereign — direct runtime dependencies (source spec for pip-compile).
#
# This is the INPUT. The hash-pinned, fully-resolved output lives beside it at
# sovereign.lock.txt and is what a sovereign deployment installs:
#
#     pip install --require-hashes -r infra/supply-chain/sovereign.lock.txt
#
# Regenerate FROM THE REPO ROOT, under Python 3.13. Both constraints are real: the lock is
# Python-minor specific, and pip-compile writes its `# via -r <path>` annotations relative to
# the directory it ran in, so regenerating from elsewhere yields a byte-different file and a
# spurious staleness failure.
#
#     cd <repo root>
#     pip install pip-tools==7.6.1
#     pip-compile --generate-hashes --no-header --strip-extras \
#                 --output-file=infra/supply-chain/sovereign.lock.txt \
#                 infra/supply-chain/sovereign.in
#
# The "A14 supply-chain gate" CI job re-runs that command against the committed lock and
# fails on drift. See docs/SUPPLY-CHAIN.md.
#
# SCOPE. env-sovereign is the offense-free personal core: vigil_core + apps/sigil +
# integration (envs/sovereign.txt). Only THIRD-PARTY deps are locked here — the three
# first-party members are installed `-e` from the tree and carry no registry hash.
# INVARIANT: nothing here may drag in framework.* (CRUCIBLE) or strix.*; that absence is
# what makes sigil.reuse.assert_no_offense() hold by construction (FATAL-2).
#
# NOT locked here (deliberate): apps/sigil's optional extras (voice / secrets / capture /
# dev). They are lazy-imported, degrade gracefully, and are not part of the default
# deployed surface. Locking them would pin a large optional tree that no default install
# pulls. `dev` extras are CI tooling, pinned in the workflow itself.

# --- apps/sigil runtime (single source of truth: apps/sigil/requirements.txt, which is
# --- kept in sync with the `dependencies` table of apps/sigil/pyproject.toml) ---
-r ../../apps/sigil/requirements.txt

# --- packages/core/vigil_core (the shared integrity substrate) ---
# Both are already constrained tighter by apps/sigil above; they are restated because
# vigil_core is independently installable and these are ITS declared floors.
cryptography>=50
pydantic>=2.10,<3
